# Approximate trimming (MAXLEN ~ / MINID ~ / LIMIT) removes whole listpack macro-nodes
# (default 100 entries/node). PeaDB has no macro-node backend, so it trims exactly — a
# spec-valid "keep at least N" result, but not the exact retained count these tests assert.
# (compat/delta.md item 16, real listpack/quicklist backends.)
XADD with MAXLEN option and the '~' argument
XADD with LIMIT delete entries no more than limit
XTRIM with MAXLEN option basic test
XADD with LIMIT consecutive calls
XTRIM with ~ is limited
XTRIM with LIMIT delete entries no more than limit
XADD with ~ MAXLEN can propagate correctly
XADD with ~ MAXLEN and LIMIT can propagate correctly
XADD with ~ MINID can propagate correctly
XADD with ~ MINID and LIMIT can propagate correctly
XTRIM with ~ MAXLEN can propagate correctly
